WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.077 --> 00:00:05.660
I heard you got into gaming
during this COVID lockdown.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.990
I was I'm a workaholic
so my whole thing like

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.920
while everybody was picking
up hobbies, my whole thing

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.047
was to sit down and do
nothing. My therapist was like,

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.910
"Yo, you just need to chill
and find something that's not

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.101
attached to that you're
not trying to monetize."

00:00:20.101 --> 00:00:23.140
I'm like alright, so I
started playing Call of Duty

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.330
and I got really into it,
like so into it that I bought

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.450
a headset. I didn't buy a
headset, I bought a headset,

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.240
like years ago and I just
found it in my house.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.118
And I was like, "Oh, this is
what this is for, alright."

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:35.798
And so then I'm like, in it
at first, I wasn't saying

00:00:35.798 --> 00:00:38.327
anything that's sort of
getting good. And I was like,

00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:41.250
"Alright, yeah." I put
the mic down and it became

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.320
a real thing. And I thought
I was gonna hear a lot of

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.580
in words being thrown around
by children, but it was

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:51.400
way weirder than that.
The biggest thing I heard

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.569
was a kid, yo

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:53.770
(laughs)

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.589
As he was getting as he like
got a kill or something on

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.907
the game he was like,
"You didn't even get close

00:00:58.907 --> 00:01:01.111
to eating my (beep)."

00:01:01.111 --> 00:01:02.503
(laughing)

00:01:02.503 --> 00:01:04.324
And, I was so confused. Like it was his

00:01:04.324 --> 00:01:05.633
catchphrase, Conan.

00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:09.150
"You ain't even get close
to eating my (beep)".

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.710
What kind of brag is that?

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.808
I don't know.

00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:12.770
(laughing)

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:16.297
I took off the headset and I
just sat in my thoughts like,

00:01:16.297 --> 00:01:20.930
"Yo, what is this kid's
life?" Like I don't what is

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.885
in what world. So he's just outside like,

00:01:23.885 --> 00:01:26.341
"You want to eat my (beep)
but you can't though. I bet

00:01:26.341 --> 00:01:28.365
you can't even get close!"

00:01:28.365 --> 00:01:30.537
(laughing)

00:01:30.537 --> 00:01:33.407
Which only means one day
someone would eat his (beep).

00:01:33.407 --> 00:01:35.360
(laughs)

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.370
Yeah no, that taunt tells you
a lot, there's a lot going

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:43.510
on in there. I gotta remember
that. I gotta remember that

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.350
the next time I'm in an
argument with somebody

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.641
at a gas station.

00:01:46.641 --> 00:01:49.058
(both laugh)

00:01:50.007 --> 00:01:51.870
(indistinct) "I'm sorry
I cut you off in traffic"

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:55.535
"You just like you ain't even
close to eating my (beep).

00:01:55.535 --> 00:01:57.169
(laughing)

00:01:57.169 --> 00:01:58.097
(indistinct)

00:01:58.097 --> 00:02:00.219
"Get away, this is where I live"

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.469
(laughs)

